"qBackups": "Before every change the previous Xray config is saved here (last 40). Restore tests it first and only brings back the Xray config; panel users and settings are not touched.",
"qCPort": "This port opens on the middle servers and this server dials it; open it in their firewall if they have one (UDP for kcp and quic).",
"qDomain": "Optional. If the middle server cannot reach this server, this server dials the middle server itself (reverse path). Without a domain only REALITY is tried; with a domain and SSL, WS and XHTTP too. Not used in user links.",
"qFrag": "The first TLS message goes out in small pieces; some filters only block when they see the site name in one whole packet. One switch for WS and XHTTP on every middle server.",
"qGre": "GRE is protocol 47, not TCP or UDP; if a firewall or the datacenter blocks it, rotation moves on to the next method.",
"qPubIP": "GRE links two public IPs directly, so the middle server's IP is needed from the start. If the SSH field holds an IP, that one is used.",
"qRaw": "The current Xray config file as it is on the server; view only, edit through this panel.",
"qRevPorts": "These ports open on the middle server and this server dials them on the reverse path. By default they match this server's tunnel ports (when free on the middle server).",
"qRtT": "The site the REALITY tunnel looks like a visit to, on this server and, on the reverse path, on the middle server. It can differ from your inbounds' sites. Needs TLS 1.3, h2 and X25519: Check tests it from this server and the middle servers.",
"qSingle": "This inbound (SOCKS or HTTP) has no client list, just one username and password, so everyone uses this one link. Link form: http://user:pass@server:port (for SOCKS, user:pass is base64). Works in any app with a proxy setting, or v2rayN/NekoBox. Not encrypted.",
"qSni": "For games and sites that refuse Iranian addresses, with no VPN. A user sets their phone's or console's DNS to an entry server's IP; only the domains in this list pass through that server, the rest of the internet stays direct. Only addresses of users who pressed Activate on their subscription page can use it. Ports 53, 80 and 443 must be free on that server. It does not get around filtering and the site name is visible.",
"qStart": "Only for the first connection. Once the middle server is connected, the other methods join the rotation too. If WS, XHTTP and REALITY are blocked, pick WireGuard or mKCP (over UDP) or GRE. FRP, Backhaul and SSH join after it connects.",
"qXu": "Checks GitHub for a new Xray once a day. It updates only when you press the button: the current config is tested with the new version first, and a failed test only warns.",
